  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Arteries, Veins & Capillaries"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Arteries"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Carry blood at **high pressure away from the heart**\n- Carry **oxygenated** blood (other than the pulmonary artery)\n- Have **thick muscular walls** containing elastic fibres\n- Have a **narrow lumen**\n- Speed of flow is **fast**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Veins"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Carry blood at **low pressure towards the heart**\n- Carry **deoxygenated** blood (other than the pulmonary vein)\n- Have **thin **walls\n- Have a **large lumen**\n- Contain **valves**\n- Speed of flow is **slow**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/01/Comparing-arteries-and-veins.png",
   "file": "assets/614ee68dfcc3-comparing-arteries-and-veins.png",
   "alt": "Comparing arteries and veins, IGCSE & GCSE Biology revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Comparing arteries and veins***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Capillaries"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Carry blood at **low pressure** within tissues\n- Carry **both oxygenated and deoxygenated blood**\n- Have walls that are **one cell thick**\n- Have ‘leaky’ walls\n- Speed of flow is **slow**"
  },
